From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Speed up the drawers

The C versions of the assembly drawers kept everything in globals and
counted every pixel for a debugging feature. They keep their state in
registers now, the wall drawer does two columns at a time with a halfword
per row, the floor drawer two pixels a loop with one shift less for each,
and the pixel counter is gone. Drawers given no pixels to draw draw none.

Ken's reciprocals read the exponent and mantissa of an integer turned
into a float, which the ARM can only do in software: floatbits() works
out the same bits with a count of leading zeros, rounded like the
conversion. The depth of the sloped floor drawer is an integer again,
like in Ken's C version, instead of a float added to every 8 pixels.
